<LegalLayout title="Support - Mute: Life Clock & Focus" description="Support and help for the Mute: Life Clock & Focus iOS app.">
  <p class="eyebrow">Mute: Life Clock &amp; Focus</p>
  <h1>Support</h1>

  <p>Mute: Life Clock &amp; Focus is a local-only iPhone app for calm focus. It shows your life clock, keeps a private mute and focus ledger, and uses Apple Screen Time controls so you can shield or silence the apps you choose on your own device.</p>

  <h2>Common questions</h2>

  <h2>Do I need an account?</h2>
  <p>No. There&rsquo;s no sign-up and no login. Just open the app and use it on your phone.</p>

  <h2>Where is my data stored?</h2>
  <p>Your date of birth, mute and focus ledger, and Apple Screen Time app-selection token are stored locally on your device. There is no server, and the developer cannot see your data. See our <a href="/mute/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> for details.</p>

  <h2>Can the app see which apps I selected?</h2>
  <p>No. Apple gives the app an opaque token for your chosen apps. The app uses that token on your device, but it never learns the names of the apps you selected, and the token never leaves your device.</p>

  <h2>Why does the app ask for Screen Time authorization?</h2>
  <p>The app uses Apple&rsquo;s Screen Time and Family Controls frameworks to shield or silence your own chosen apps. Authorization is handled by Apple on your device.</p>

  <h2>Does the app use analytics or ads?</h2>
  <p>No. The app has no analytics SDK, no ads, no tracking, no account, and no third-party data sharing.</p>

  <h2>What happens if I delete the app?</h2>
  <p>Deleting the app deletes the data stored by the app on your device.</p>

  <h2>Need more help?</h2>
  <p>Email us at <a href="mailto:support@mikhailnarbekov.com">support@mikhailnarbekov.com</a>. We aim to reply within a few business days.</p>
</LegalLayout>
